  "notes": "Letter and number contacts are each labelled on their own side, so every contact is its own entry (pin = the contact, also = the opposite contact). Where both sides carry the same words the drawing does not say whether they are paralleled or the two legs of a balanced signal; polarity is left null. MIC on A and 1 with MIC SHIELD on 2 looks like a balanced mic input (A/1 = the two legs) but no +/- is drawn. RS1, FB2, FB1, AUX1-4, PFL and SOLO are the mix/cue buses (direction onto the bus not drawn). PRE OUT (Z/22) with LINE IN (U/17) and BOOSTER IN (W/19) may form a patch point, but nothing on the page calls it an insert, so no insert is recorded. Legend: NC = not connected, IC = internally connected. Page numbers 4-1 (P1, marked UPPER) and 4-2 (P2, marked LOWER). No title block, date or drawing number on the page. This picture is page 4-2, P2 only. Y = +24V but 21 = +25V as drawn."
